---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="What this website collects about visitors, and how to stop it.">
  <div class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-8">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-4">
        This notice covers this website, productbuildershq.com. It has no accounts, no forms and no advertising.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Analytics</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-4">
        We count page views with PostHog, in its EU cloud. It runs in a cookieless mode: it sets no cookies and
        stores nothing in your browser. From your IP address and browser details it computes an identifier that
        changes every day, so a visit is counted once per day; the address itself is not kept. We see totals such
        as page views, the pages read and the sites that sent visitors, not who you are, and it does not follow
        you across other sites.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-4">
        If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, the analytics do not load at all.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Cookies and storage</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-4">This website sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser.</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Hosting</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-4">
        Like any website, the servers that deliver these pages briefly process standard request information, such
        as your IP address and browser type, to deliver and protect the site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
